    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nCurrently split in two units, commercial on the ground floor and living accommodation on the first, with a little imagination this attractive bay windowed property could be transformed back to a spacious, functioning family home. Ideally positioned in a very convenient location on the Malahide Road in Artane and extending to approximately 139sq.m (1,496sq.ft) with a large garden to the rear (approximately 66 feet), there is also the added benefit of off-street parking to the front. \n\nThe property benefits from full planning permission to convert back to full residential use, including permission for an extension and the construction of a self-contained unit at the rear.\n\nPlanning Reference - WEB2219/25.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises entrance porch, hallway, four receptions rooms, guest wc and storage on the ground floor level. Upstairs (originally a four bed) is now laid out in three bedrooms, kitchen, bathroom and separate wc. The cobble lock driveway to the front provides secure off-street parking. There is a large garden to the rear, mainly laid in lawn, with great potential to extend the property further (subject to pp). \n \nNo. 43 Malahide Road is situated close to all local shops, amenities and excellent primary & secondary schools. Both Killester and Clontarf Village are within walking distance and offer fine restaurants, bars, cafes, boutiques and recreational facilities as well as St Anne's Park and Dollymount Strand. There are numerous transport links close to the property including the DART service from Harmonstown station and several bus routes in the immediate area. Dublin Airport, Beaumont Hospital, the M50, M1, and the city centre are also easily accessible.\n \n****Viewing is strictly by appointment****\n \nIf you'd like to arrange a viewing, please email me directly or contact the office on 01 8336555 and we'd be happy to set something up."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Attractive semi-detached residence </li><li>Currently split in two units commercial and residential </li><li>Full planning to revert to residential use reference- WEB2219/25</li><li>Extended and spacious </li><li>Double glazing</li><li>Gas fired central heating</li><li>Off-street parking</li><li>Large rear garden (L 66 ft x W 34 ft)</li><li>Very convenient location </li><li>Within 4.5km of the city centre</ul>"
      },
